// The Enochian tablets: the four Watchtowers, thirteen rows of twelve
// letters, and the Tablet of Union, four rows of five, as each source
// prints them. A version of a tablet (the Golden Dawn's, Regardie's, the
// Equinox's, Dee's or Raphael's) is a rule over these readings, not a copy
// of them: magick-data/enochian/tablets's `tabletVersion()` applies it
// (plan 061, "Tablet versions").
//
// `readings` holds each source's letters, keyed by source:
//   regardie1940  Israel Regardie, *The Golden Dawn*, vol. 4 (Aries Press,
//                 Chicago, 1940), the Book of the Concourse of the Forces:
//                 archive.org item IsraelRegardie-TheGoldenDawn-Vol4-1940,
//                 Air p.270 (leaf n262), Water p.271 (n263), Earth p.272
//                 (n264), Fire p.273 (n265), the Tablet of Union's lines
//                 p.275 (n267).
//   equinox1912   *The Equinox*, vol. I no. 7 (London, 1912), "Liber
//                 Chanokh", Plates III and VIII: archive.org item
//                 crowley-equinox_202110, file "The Equinox Vol. 1, No. 7",
//                 leaves n241 and n246.
//   greer         The Watchtowers redrawn in Regardie, *The Golden Dawn*,
//                 7th edition, ed. John Michael Greer (Llewellyn, ISBN
//                 978-0-7387-4399-8), its colour plates "Enochian Tablet:
//                 The First Watchtower" to "The Fourth Watchtower".
//   dee1584       Dee and Kelley's tables of June 1584 as Casaubon prints
//                 Dee's record, *A True & Faithful Relation* (London, 1659;
//                 from British Library, Cotton MS Appendix XLVI): archive.org
//                 item truefaithfulrela00deej, pp.175-177 (leaves
//                 n264-n266), with Dee's corrections (pp.185 and 188, leaves
//                 n274 and n277).
//   raphael1587   The Tabula recensa of 20 April 1587, "thus reformed by
//                 Raphael", in the same book's "Actio Tertia", second
//                 pagination, p.15 (leaf n456).
// Dee's records name the four tables by their middle rows; the Golden Dawn
// gives them elements: ORO is Air, MPH Water, MOR Earth and OIP Fire. Dee
// and Raphael have no Tablet of Union, which is the Golden Dawn's.
//
// A reading's `rows` run from the top, one character a square: the Latin
// transliteration, a capital where the source prints one, and "." for a
// square the source leaves empty. Where a source prints more than one
// letter in a square, `rows` has the higher, first one. `marks` names, by
// row and column from 0, the squares that hold more:
//   beside    letters printed on the same line, after the first (Regardie
//             prints y and l side by side in Water's row 5, square 12);
//   below     the smaller letters printed below (Regardie's second
//             letters: u over v is "u" in `rows` and below ["v"]);
//   reversed  the square's letter is printed reversed (the Equinox writes
//             these in Enochian, Greer mirrors them);
//   dictated  the letters first written down in the 1584 session, where Dee
//             later corrected the square and `rows` has his correction;
//   misprint  what the 1659 print has, where every other copy of Dee's
//             tables read (his 1584 table and the 1587 table's copies)
//             agrees on the letter in `rows`; the Golden Dawn's sources
//             are not counted;
//   alt       other readings of the square in this version's witnesses: the
//             1587 letters for the two Fire squares the 1584 record leaves
//             empty, and Sloane MS 3191's p where the 1587 print has x;
//   doubt     how sure the reading is: "low", "medium" or "high" doubt.
// Rows and squares are counted from 1 in the comments below, from 0 in the
// data.
//
// `choices.gd` is the Golden Dawn's version: Regardie's higher letter,
// which he prefers while allowing both (p.306, leaf n298), except in the
// squares listed, where both other sources print another letter and the
// Order's names through the square read it too (the Seniors as the Greer
// edition's "The Four Elemental Weapons" names them; the names Liber
// Chanokh reads off Water, The Equinox, pp.235-236). There the version
// takes the Equinox's letter. Water's row 5 square 12 has no higher letter
// to take: Regardie prints four there, y and l side by side over N and h,
// and the version takes N, one of his four, which both other sources print
// (reversed). That differs from Water's row 5 square 1 and row 12 square 1,
// where he prints two letters, one plainly higher (f over p, r over i):
// the higher stands there although both other sources print the lower,
// since no name settles them. The version's reversed letters are the
// Equinox's, and its other letters in a square (its `alt`) are every other
// letter any of the three Golden Dawn sources prints there. Plan 061
// (Stage G notes) lists every square where those sources differ.
//
// Dee's version is the 1584 table as Dee corrected it, which the angel
// approved (p.188): in four squares, where the session's record has a
// letter that every later copy replaces, it takes the later letter and
// keeps the first as `dictated`. Its case is Casaubon's type, and its
// reversed letters are marked as he prints or notes them, except Earth's
// row 8 square 1, a reversed R, which he sets as the ligature Æ: the
// reading has R, reversed (doubt medium). Two Fire squares (row 1 square
// 12 and row 2 square 11) are empty in every 1584 witness read: they are
// kept empty, with the 1587 letters as `alt`.
// Raphael's version follows the 1659 print of the 1587 table, small letters
// as printed: the capitals of Sloane MS 3191's copy are unverified until
// its images return (plan 061). In Fire's row 8 square 1 and row 12 square
// 4 the print (from the Cotton manuscript) has x, Sloane p. Of its ten
// misprints, Fire's row 6 square 8 is the least sure: the print's v is
// Regardie's second letter there (b over v), so it may be the Cotton
// copy's reading rather than the printer's slip (doubt medium).
//
// Cross-checked, never cited: J. H. Peterson's redraws of Sloane MS 3191
// (esotericarchives.com) and the Vovina Archives' renderings of the Cotton
// and Sloane tables (CC BY-NC-SA 4.0). Nothing of theirs is copied here.
// The letters are facts, and no rights are asserted over them.
